        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="350819511">
          <groundspeak:date>2013-08-21T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1390708">canoecolt</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP466    Sawridge Creek

N55° 16.552     W114° 46.288&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Well, this was a FIRST for us a BRASS CAP Cache.  In the U.S. we have found several benchmarks but received a first rate lesson in Brass Cap Caching from DRONNORD.  Headed down the trail with shovel and survey taped stick, we made it to GZ.  Interesting although, I doubt we would have found it on our own.  Bonus was we spotted a black bear in the bend of the creek down below.  He stayed and was curious about us for a few candid shots before slowling sauntering around the bend south.  Thanks outforthehunt and dronnord for a fascinating new facet of geocaching. TFTF!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This entry was edited by canoecolt on Wednesday, 18 September 2013 at 05:24:32 UTC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
